{number: 77}
{title: When We Walk with the Lord}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
When we [F] walk with the Lord in the [C7] light of His [F] Word
What a glory He [C7] sheds on our [F] way!
While we do His good will, He a-[C7] bides with us [F] still,
And with all who will [C7] trust and o-[F] bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C7] Trust and o-[F] bey, for there's [D7] no other [Gm] way
To be [F] happy in [Dm] Jesus,
But to [F] trust [C7] and o-[F] bey.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Not a [F] shadow can rise, not a [C7] cloud in the [F] skies,
But His smile quickly [C7] drives it a-[F] way;
Not a doubt or a fear, not a [C7] sigh nor a [F] tear,
Can abide while we [C7] trust and o-[F] bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
But we [F] never can prove the de-[C7] lights of His [F] love
Until all on the [C7] altar we [F] lay;
For the favor He shows, and the [C7] joy He be-[F] stows,
Are for them who will [C7] trust and o-[F] bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then in [F] fellowship sweet we will [C7] sit at His [F] feet,
Or we'll walk by His [C7] side in the [F] way;
What He says we will do, where He [C7] sends we will [F] go,--
Never fear, only [C7] trust and o-[F] bey.
{end_of_verse}
